+## Planned controlled CPU/GPU comparison (not executed)
+
+The frozen-for-review [comparison protocol v1](CPU_GPU_COMPARISON_PROTOCOL_v1.md)
+and [exact matrix](studies/cpu_gpu_comparison_v1.matrix.json) specify 48 datasets
+at N1025/65537/1000000: five seeded distributions with seeds1729/42/2718 plus one
+nonrandom signed-edge dataset per size. Three CPU modes (std_sort, merge_sort,
+two-thread parallel_merge_sort), production CUB and prepared CUB use balanced
+five-round ordering. W1/R5 gives 1200 measured invocations and 240 warm-ups, with
+four diagnostics per prepared invocation. A separate six-dataset pilot is required.
+
+The primary `host_vector_api_call_v1` scope times the unchanged public sorter from
+restored ordinary vector to complete host-visible result. It includes internal
+allocation/free and production CUDA pageable transfers, dispatch and checked
+synchronization; excludes input restoration, context initialization, oracle and
+validation. Existing prepared H2D/device/D2H/end-to-end scopes are preserved and
+cannot supply CPU speedup denominators. CPU and GPU calls must run on the same
+Colab VM/build/input. Cross-seed aggregation weights distinct dataset medians;
+repetitions are not independent datasets. All outliers remain.
+
+[Resource estimates](studies/cpu_gpu_comparison_v1.resources.csv) include simultaneous
+prepared and production buffers. At 1M, known host payload is 24MB; device keys
+are 16MB plus two unknown CUB workspaces. Each has a 64MiB policy allowance, not a
+measured bound. Fresh queries, headroom checks and a pilot replace planning time
+assumptions before execution. The new driver/schema/analyzer are specified but
+not implemented; no runnable comparison command or performance result is claimed.
+See the [freeze hashes](studies/cpu_gpu_comparison_v1.freeze.json) and
+[planning audit](../results/raw/cpu_gpu_protocol_20261009T234954580281Z/FINAL_AUDIT.md).
